    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5db905514ac709676430d1e0aa78cae438ba13ba1c9329c991306f798704ed85",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Fourier support acts as a common analytic resource parameter in three distinct parts of the argument: under contour motion it controls the exponential growth of the complex-shifted test function and hence the residue and terminal-line errors; in the local expansion it decides whether frequency one can contribute a visible 1/log X term; and in the odd-prime contribution it sets the cutoff Y = X^sigma whose length must be offset by character-sum cancellation. Comparing the Jutila and Poisson treatments further shows that changing the cancellation machinery changes the resulting error-versus-support tradeoff.",
